# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# .gitignore — MDT-OEM-Extensibility
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# This repository ships build tooling, per-vendor recipes, and small
# customization assets. It does NOT ship vendor installers, downloaded
# caches, or built .7z archives — those are regenerated by the build tools
# from official sources.
#
# The rules below enforce that separation. Sections 1 through 3 cover the
# artifacts that must never be committed. Sections 4 through 9 cover the
# standard junk. Sections 10 and 11 re-include the small assets that ARE
# part of the repository.
#
# If you find yourself needing to commit a file this .gitignore excludes,
# read CONTRIBUTING.md first. Committing vendor binaries is almost always
# the wrong answer — open an issue and explain why the recipe approach
# does not work for your case.
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. DOWNLOAD CACHE AND STAGING
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The build tool downloads installers into a content-addressed cache and
# stages them before packing. Neither the cache nor the staging area should
# ever be committed. They are large and regenerable.

cache/
Cache/
.cache/
BuildCache/

staging/
Staging/
.build/
Output/
output/

# Tool-specific scratch space
Temp/
tmp/
.tmp/
scratch/
Scratch/


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. BUILT ARCHIVES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The output of Build-OEMPack.ps1. These are what users distribute to their
# deployment share — not what lives in Git.

*.7z
*.7z.001
*.7z.002
*.7z.003
*.7z.004
*.7z.005
*.7z.006
*.7z.007
*.7z.008
*.7z.009
*.7z.010
*.rar
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# Exception: small sample archives used for testing the tool itself.
!tests/fixtures/*.7z
!tests/fixtures/*.zip

# Exception: vendor recipe files that might be distributed as archives
# for external use. Only allow small ones under docs/examples.
!docs/examples/*.zip


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. VENDOR INSTALLERS AND DOWNLOADS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never commit a vendor installer or driver package. They are downloaded
# at build time from official sources, verified by hash, and cached locally.
# The repository ships the recipe, not the binary.

# Executables and installers
*.exe
*.com
*.scr
*.msi
*.msp
*.msu
*.msix
*.msixbundle
*.msixupload
*.appx
*.appxbundle
*.appxupload
*.msi.deploy

# Drivers
*.sys
*.inf
*.cat
*.dll
*.ocx
*.cpl

# Firmware and BIOS updates
*.bin
*.rom
*.efi
*.cap
*.fd

# Windows update packages
*.cab
*.psf

# Disk and OS images
*.iso
*.wim
*.esd
*.swm
*.vhd
*.vhdx
*.avhdx
*.vmdk
*.vdi
*.ffu


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. LOGS AND BUILD OUTPUT
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build logs, error transcripts, and any JSON emitted as a side effect of
# running the tools. The only JSON committed is the intentional recipe and
# schema files.

*.log
*.etl
*.evtx

# Build manifest output (produced by Test-OEMAppPack.ps1)
BuildReport.json
ValidationReport.json
*.build.json

# winget download scratch
winget-download-*.json
winget-download-*.yaml
winget-download-*.txt


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5. TEMPORARY AND BACKUP FILES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.old
*.orig
*.rej
*.crdownload
*.partial
*.part
~$*
*.dmp

# Editor auto-save artifacts
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
*~


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 6. WINDOWS OPERATING SYSTEM JUNK
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk
*.url
*.stackdump
[Dd]esktop.ini


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 7. macOS AND LINUX JUNK
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 8. EDITOR AND IDE FILES
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

.vscode/
!.vscode/settings.json.example
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json.example

.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace

.vs/
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

*.code-workspace


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 9. POWERSHELL ARTIFACTS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

*.ps1xml
PSScriptAnalyzerSettings.psd1.local
TestResults.xml
CodeCoverage.xml
*.Tests.ps1.bak
*.psd1.local


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 10. SECRETS AND MACHINE-SPECIFIC CONFIGURATION
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Local overrides of any tracked configuration
*.local.*
!*.local.example
!*.local.template

# Product keys, credentials, and license files
*productkey*
*ProductKey*
*serial*
*license.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
secrets.json
credentials.json

# Personal scratch files
*.personal.*
*.private.*
*.draft.*


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 11. VENDOR ASSETS — EXPLICIT RE-INCLUDE
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The small customization assets committed per vendor. These are checked
# in under vendors/<Vendor>/Assets/. They total a few megabytes per vendor
# and change infrequently.
#
# What is allowed here:
#   - Customization scripts (Customizations.ps1 and similar)
#   - Registry files (.reg)
#   - Configuration files (.xml, .json, .txt, .ini)
#   - Wallpapers and theme assets (.jpg, .png, .bmp, .theme)
#   - Vendor-specific unattend.xml overlays
#   - Manifest fragments used by the framework

# Scripts and configuration
!vendors/*/Assets/**
!vendors/*/Assets/*.ps1
!vendors/*/Assets/*.psm1
!vendors/*/Assets/*.reg
!vendors/*/Assets/*.xml
!vendors/*/Assets/*.json
!vendors/*/Assets/*.txt
!vendors/*/Assets/*.ini
!vendors/*/Assets/*.csv

# Wallpapers and theme assets
!vendors/*/Assets/*.jpg
!vendors/*/Assets/*.jpeg
!vendors/*/Assets/*.png
!vendors/*/Assets/*.bmp
!vendors/*/Assets/*.ico
!vendors/*/Assets/*.theme
!vendors/*/Assets/*.themepack

# Nested asset folders
!vendors/*/Assets/**/*.jpg
!vendors/*/Assets/**/*.jpeg
!vendors/*/Assets/**/*.png
!vendors/*/Assets/**/*.bmp
!vendors/*/Assets/**/*.ico
!vendors/*/Assets/**/*.theme
!vendors/*/Assets/**/*.ps1
!vendors/*/Assets/**/*.psm1
!vendors/*/Assets/**/*.reg
!vendors/*/Assets/**/*.xml
!vendors/*/Assets/**/*.txt
!vendors/*/Assets/**/*.ini

# Note: binary files with large sizes inside Assets are still a bad idea.
# If an asset exceeds a few megabytes, consider whether it belongs in the
# repo. Wallpapers are typically 1-5 MB and acceptable; anything over 10 MB
# per file should be questioned.


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 12. RECIPES, SCHEMAS, AND TOOLING — EXPLICIT RE-INCLUDE
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The core content of the repository. These must always be tracked.

!vendors/*/Recipe.json
!vendors/*/README.md
!vendors/*/Overrides/**
!schema/**
!schema/*.json
!tools/**
!tools/*.ps1
!tools/*.psm1
!docs/**
!docs/**/*.md
!docs/images/**
!tests/**
!tests/**/*.ps1
!tests/fixtures/**

# Keep .gitkeep placeholders so empty directory structures are tracked.
!.gitkeep
!**/.gitkeep


# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 13. GIT INTERNAL BACKUPS
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

.gitattributes.bak
.gitmodules.bak
*.orig.git
*.orig.gitignore


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# END OF .gitignore
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# If you need to force-add a file that this file ignores, use:
#
#     git add -f <file>
#
# and explain WHY in your commit message and pull request description.
# The reviewer will decide whether the file belongs in the tracked set.
#
# Common cases that require force-add and usually indicate a mistake:
#
#   - An installer (.exe, .msi, .msix) — the recipe should fetch it instead
#   - A built archive (.7z) — regenerable from the recipe
#   - A large wallpaper (over 10 MB) — consider compressing or resizing
#
# Common cases that should NOT require force-add:
#
#   - A new vendor recipe — commit normally
#   - A customization script — commit normally
#   - A small registry file — commit normally
#   - A wallpaper under vendors/<Vendor>/Assets/ — commit normally
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
